From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:48:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb: core: hub: don't enable U1 on a link tunnelled over USB4

USB4 does not support U1 on a USB3 link that is tunnelled through a
USB4 router (USB4 v2.0 section 9.2.1.1); only U2 is available there.
usb_enable_lpm() still enables hub-initiated U1 on such a link when the
port permits it.

Skip hub-initiated U1 when the host reports the device's link as
tunnelled. usb_enable_lpm() enables device-initiated U2 only together
with device-initiated U1, so when the device may not initiate U1 on a
tunnelled link, enable device-initiated U2 on its own, provided
hub-initiated U2 is enabled and the device may initiate it.

This affects every host that reports the tunnel state, including Intel
xHCIs with USB4: U1 is no longer enabled on the root port link to a
device behind a USB4 tunnel. Native links and hosts that cannot tell
are unchanged.

Assisted-by: Opus 5.5
Signed-off-by: Jim Martin <jimmartin@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/core/hub.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
index b446905b48b..61f5cc5f802 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/core/hub.c
@@ -4523,6 +4523,7 @@ void usb_enable_lpm(struct usb_device *udev)
 	struct usb_hcd *hcd;
 	struct usb_hub *hub;
 	struct usb_port *port_dev;
+	bool tunneled;
 
 	if (!udev || !udev->parent ||
 			udev->speed < USB_SPEED_SUPER ||
@@ -4548,7 +4549,10 @@ void usb_enable_lpm(struct usb_device *udev)
 
 	port_dev = hub->ports[udev->portnum - 1];
 
-	if (port_dev->usb3_lpm_u1_permit)
+	/* USB4 does not support U1 on USB3 links tunneled over it. */
+	tunneled = udev->tunnel_mode == USB_LINK_TUNNELED;
+
+	if (port_dev->usb3_lpm_u1_permit && !tunneled)
 		if (usb_enable_link_state(hcd, udev, USB3_LPM_U1))
 			return;
 
@@ -4566,6 +4570,9 @@ void usb_enable_lpm(struct usb_device *udev)
 
 		if (usb_device_may_initiate_lpm(udev, USB3_LPM_U2))
 			usb_set_device_initiated_lpm(udev, USB3_LPM_U2, true);
+	} else if (tunneled && udev->usb3_lpm_u2_enabled &&
+		   usb_device_may_initiate_lpm(udev, USB3_LPM_U2)) {
+		usb_set_device_initiated_lpm(udev, USB3_LPM_U2, true);
 	}
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(usb_enable_lpm);
-- 
